---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
const updated = 'November 2026';
---
<Base title="Privacy policy" description="How AIForgeWorx collects, uses and protects personal information.">
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p>Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <!-- TEMPLATE: review this with a lawyer before publishing, and update it if
           you add analytics, newsletters or other tools that collect information. -->

      <p>
        {site.legalName} (“we”) respects your privacy. This policy explains what personal
        information we collect through this website, why, and how we protect it, in line with
        Canada’s Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act (PIPEDA) and
        British Columbia’s Personal Information Protection Act (PIPA).
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>This website has no forms or sign-ups. We collect only what you choose to send us by email:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name, email address and organization</li>
        <li>the contents of your message</li>
      </ul>
      <p>This site doesn’t use advertising or tracking cookies.</p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>
        We use your information only to respond to your enquiry and, if we work together, to
        manage that engagement. We don’t sell or rent personal information, and we don’t use it
        for marketing unless you ask us to.
      </p>

      <h2>Service providers</h2>
      <p>
        This site is hosted on GitHub Pages, which may keep standard server logs, such as IP
        addresses, for security purposes. Email is handled by our email provider. These
        providers are bound by their own privacy and security commitments.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep enquiries for up to two years, or longer if we enter into an engagement and the
        information forms part of that business record.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see, correct or delete the personal information we hold about you, or
        withdraw your consent to our using it. Email us at
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we’ll respond within 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions or complaints</h2>
      <p>
        Contact our privacy officer at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. If you’re
        not satisfied with our response, you can contact the Office of the Information and Privacy
        Commissioner for British Columbia or the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
